Id: path012i
Severity: INFO
Category: accounts
Check: check_path

A directory on a user's PATH can be written by its group or by any
user. Whoever can write the directory can drop in a Trojan horse under
the name of a command the user runs. Remove the write permission, or
take the directory out of the PATH.

It is INFO because the file named is a directory or not executable,
though others (its group, or anyone) can write it.

Until 3.4.0 this was reported as path007; the number changed because
path007w meant something else in older versions.
